{"text": "If we understand mass culture. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> As a weakening factor of the cultural ties. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That unite people to their traditions. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Mass culture weakens the intermediary institutions in society. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> E, g, the family or the school. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Diminishing their role. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And overlapping these institutions. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For example. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Courts are traditional social institutions. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And important for the normal and harmonious functioning of collective life. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> However. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> When people turn to social networks. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To put pressure on judicial decisions. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In certain mediated and politicized processes. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> This practice is popularized. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And becomes a habitual form of culture. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Which is harmful. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Justice must not be done in the public square. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Which today is converted into a virtual dimension. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The social networks. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In a democratic state of law. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The appropriate place to judge and make justice. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Is the court. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And in a way that is immune to popular pressure.", "alignment": {"characters": ["I", "f", " ", "w", "e", " ", "u", "n", "d", "e", "r", "s", "t", "a", "n", "d", " ", "m", "a", "s", "s", " ", "c", "u", "l", "t", "u", "r", "e", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "A", "s", " ", "a", " ", "w", "e", "a", "k", "e", "n", "i", "n", "g", " ", "f", "a", "c", "t", "o", "r", " ", "o", "f", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "c", "u", "l", "t", "u", "r", "a", "l", " ", "t", "i", "e", "s", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t